  "equipment_type": "Power meter gateway (electrical measurement)",
  "applies_to": "Socomec DIRIS Digiware M-50 and M-70 display/gateways and the DIRIS Digiware, DIRIS and COUNTIS devices connected downstream on RS-485 or the Digiware bus.",
  "summary": "The DIRIS Digiware M-50 / M-70 is a BACnet IP gateway for Socomec metering. Each downstream device appears as its own BACnet device (instance 100 + its Modbus address) with Analog Input objects per load: voltages, currents, unbalance, active, reactive and apparent power and power factor per phase and total, load-curve values, THD and energy counters. The object number is the load number times 100 plus a fixed measurement index (0-61); this list shows load 1.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 100,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Only the index table is printed. Instance = load number x 100 + index (load 1 = AI 100-161, load 2 = AI 200-261 and so on); load 1 is listed here.",
    "Device instances: the gateway itself is the main instance (default 100); a downstream device with Modbus address xx is device 100 + xx.",
    "A device returns 0 for measurements it does not support (for example THD on a DIRIS Digiware I-30).",
    "The manual also mentions Binary Input and Binary Output objects (auxiliary contacts, IO-10 outputs) but gives no table for them; they are not listed.",
    "The guide gives no read/write column; all listed measurement objects are read-only values.",
    "Copied from a distributor-hosted copy of the Socomec manual; socomec.com blocks automated downloads."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "DIRIS Digiware M-50 / M-70 instruction manual, Annex B BACnet communication",
    "doc_number": "548751D",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.instrumentation2000.com//media/pdf/socomec-m-50-m-70-manual.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "host": "Instrumentation2000"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Discover one BACnet device per metered device (instance 100 + Modbus address) behind the gateway, then read the per-load Analog Inputs: total power, energy, current, voltage and power factor. All values are read-only.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AI 121",
        "name": "TotalPowerActive",
        "why": "Total active power, W (load 1)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 156",
        "name": "A+",
        "why": "Imported active energy, Wh (load 1)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 102",
        "name": "CurrentSyst",
        "why": "System current, A (load 1)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 100",
        "name": "VystPhN",
        "why": "System phase-neutral voltage, V (load 1)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 124",
        "name": "TotalPowerFactor",
        "why": "Total power factor (load 1)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 103",
        "name": "Frequency",
        "why": "Frequency, Hz (load 1)"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "BACnet IP is switched on in Easy Config System or the web server (BACnet activation).",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Main instance ID defaults to 100 and must be unique; a virtual network ID must also be set and be unique.",
      "UDP port is fixed at 47808.",
      "The PICS is on socomec.com."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Object numbers repeat per load: load 2 adds 100 to every instance.",
      "Unsupported measurements read 0, not an error."
    ]
  },
